# Worker client

Import WireRead from "./wire_read.lg".
Import TrailRecord from "./trail_record.lg".
Import HostTools from "./host_tools.lg".
Import ArtifactRules from "./artifact_rules.lg".
Import CoordinatorWire from "./coordinator_wire.lg".
Import LeaseWire from "./lease_wire.lg".
Import DbTrail from "./db_trail.lg".

A worker's side of the coordinator's public API: it leases a unit, keeps the
lease alive, posts the attempt, and reads the trail and artifacts any visitor can
read. It holds no database credential and never sees the OpenRouter key; the
lease's secret is the only credential it sends.

## Note
One JSON exchange with the coordinator at `base`.

## To coordinatorCall (method: Text, url: Text, body: Text) -> Result of HttpReply and Text:
    Let mutable headers be a new Map of Text to Text.
    If body is not equal to "":
        Set headers at "content-type" to "application/json".
    Return httpCall(method, url, headers, body, 60000).

## Note
A lease on a unit, or why none was granted: a refusal, an answer that is not a
grant, or `granted: false` with the coordinator's reason.

## To leaseUnit (base: Text, r: LeaseRequest) -> Result of LeaseGrant and Text:
    Inspect coordinatorCall("POST", base + "/api/v1/lease", toJson_LeaseRequest(r)):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "the coordinator could not be reached: " + e.
        When Ok (reply):
            If reply's status is not equal to 200:
                Return a new Err with error "the lease was answered {reply's status}: " + shortenText(reply's body, 400).
            Inspect fromJson_LeaseGrant(reply's body):
                When Err (e):
                    Return a new Err with error "the grant does not decode: " + e.
                When Ok (g):
                    Return a new Ok with value g.
    Return a new Err with error "no grant".

## Note
Whether the lease `g` granted is still the worker's after a heartbeat.

## To heartbeatLease (base: Text, g: LeaseGrant, holder: Text, ttlMs: Int) -> Bool:
    Inspect g's lease:
        When None:
            Return false.
        When Some (l):
            Let h be a new HeartbeatRequest with unitId l's unitId and token l's token and holder holder and secret g's secret and ttlMs ttlMs.
            Inspect coordinatorCall("POST", base + "/api/v1/heartbeat", toJson_HeartbeatRequest(h)):
                When Err (e):
                    Return false.
                When Ok (reply):
                    Inspect fromJson_HeartbeatAnswer(reply's body):
                        When Ok (a):
                            Return reply's status is equal to 200 and a's alive.
                        When Err (e):
                            Return false.
    Return false.

## Note
What became of a posted attempt: the status, and the receipt, or a refusal's code
and detail in the receipt's `outcome` and `detail`.

## A Posted has:
    a status, which is Int.
    a receipt, which is AttemptReceipt.

## To postAttempt (base: Text, s: AttemptSubmission) -> Posted:
    Inspect coordinatorCall("POST", base + "/api/v1/attempt", toJson_AttemptSubmission(s)):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Posted with status 0 and receipt (a new AttemptReceipt with accepted false and outcome "unreachable" and detail e).
        When Ok (reply):
            If reply's status is equal to 201:
                Inspect fromJson_AttemptReceipt(reply's body):
                    When Ok (r):
                        Return a new Posted with status 201 and receipt r.
                    When Err (e):
                        Return a new Posted with status 201 and receipt (a new AttemptReceipt with accepted true and outcome "undecodable receipt" and detail e).
            Let mutable code be "refused".
            Let mutable detail be shortenText(reply's body, 400).
            Inspect parseStrict(reply's body):
                When Ok (v):
                    Set code to textAt(v, "error").
                    Set detail to textAt(v, "detail").
                When Err (e):
                    Set code to "refused".
            Return a new Posted with status reply's status and receipt (a new AttemptReceipt with accepted false and outcome code and detail detail).
    Return a new Posted with status 0 and receipt (a new AttemptReceipt with accepted false and outcome "unposted").

## Note
An artifact's text, refused unless it hashes to the name it was fetched by: the
coordinator is not trusted to serve the right bytes.

## To fetchArtifact (base: Text, sha: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Inspect coordinatorCall("GET", base + "/api/v1/artifact/" + sha, ""):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "the artifact store could not be reached: " + e.
        When Ok (reply):
            If reply's status is not equal to 200:
                Return a new Err with error "artifact {sha} was answered {reply's status}".
            If contentSha(reply's body) is not equal to sha:
                Return a new Err with error "artifact {sha} does not hash to its name".
            Return a new Ok with value reply's body.
    Return a new Err with error "no artifact".

## Note
A problem's trail as the coordinator serves it, oldest entry first.

## To fetchTrail (base: Text, problemId: Text) -> Result of Seq of TrailEntry and Text:
    Inspect coordinatorCall("GET", base + "/api/v1/trail?problem=" + problemId, ""):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "the trail could not be read: " + e.
        When Ok (reply):
            If reply's status is not equal to 200:
                Return a new Err with error "the trail was answered {reply's status}".
            Return entriesOf(reply's body).
    Return a new Err with error "no trail".
